sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / kubectl
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Webhook as Operator Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Controller as Operator Controller<br/>ModelRegistryReconciler
    participant Route as OpenShift Route / HTTPRoute<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Proxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Registry as model-registry REST<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
    participant Postgres as PostgreSQL<br/>5432/TCP

    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
        Note over User,Postgres: Flow 1: ModelRegistry Instance Deployment
        User->>K8sAPI: CREATE ModelRegistry CR<br/>Bearer Token / TLS 1.2+
        K8sAPI->>Webhook: Mutating: Default fields<br/>TLS / Admission
        Webhook-->>K8sAPI: JSON Patch
        K8sAPI->>Webhook: Validating: Check spec + name uniqueness<br/>TLS / Admission
        Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Allowed
        K8sAPI-->>User: CR Created
        K8sAPI->>Controller: Watch event: ModelRegistry added
        Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Deployment, Service, Route,<br/>NetworkPolicy, RBAC, Secrets<br/>ServiceAccount Token / TLS
        K8sAPI-->>Controller: Resources created
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
        Note over User,Postgres: Flow 2: Model Registry API Access
        User->>Route: GET /v2/registered_models<br/>HTTPS / Bearer Token
        Route->>Proxy: Forward request<br/>TLS reencrypt
        Proxy->>K8sAPI: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS / ServiceAccount
        K8sAPI-->>Proxy: Authenticated + Authorized
        Proxy->>Registry: Forward to localhost<br/>HTTP 8080/TCP (no auth)
        Registry->>Postgres: Query metadata<br/>5432/TCP Password auth
        Postgres-->>Registry: Result set
        Registry-->>Proxy: JSON response
        Proxy-->>Route: Encrypted response
        Route-->>User: JSON over HTTPS
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 230)
        Note over User,Postgres: Flow 3: Catalog Access via Gateway API
        User->>Route: GET /api/catalog/models<br/>HTTPS / Bearer Token
        Note over Route: Platform Gateway<br/>data-science-gateway
        Route->>Proxy: Forward to model-catalog<br/>TLS passthrough 8443/TCP
        Proxy->>K8sAPI: TokenReview + SubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS / ServiceAccount
        K8sAPI-->>Proxy: Authenticated + Authorized
        Proxy->>Registry: Forward to catalog service<br/>HTTP 8080/TCP (localhost)
        Note over Registry: model-catalog service
        Registry->>Postgres: Query catalog metadata<br/>5432/TCP Password auth
        Note over Postgres: model-catalog-postgres
        Postgres-->>Registry: Result set
        Registry-->>Proxy: JSON response
        Proxy-->>Route: Encrypted response
        Route-->>User: JSON over HTTPS
    end
